                "scan": "s102",
                "printed_page": "37",
                "text": "אֵל אָדוֹן עַל כָּל־הַמַּעֲשִׂים. בָּרוּךְ וּמְבֹרָךְ בְּפִי כָּל־נְשָׁמָה: גָּדְלוֹ וְטוּבוֹ מָלֵא עוֹלָם. דַּֽעַת וּתְבוּנָה סֹבְבִים אוֹתוֹ: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s102",
                "printed_page": "37",
                "text": "הַמִּתְגָּאֶה עַל־חַיּוֹת הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ. וְנֶהְדָּר בְּכָבוֹד עַל־הַמֶּרְכָּבָה:",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/2"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "זְכוּת וּמִישׁוֹר לִפְנֵי כִסְאוֹ. חֶֽסֶד וְרַחֲמִים לִפְנֵי כְבוֹדוֹ: ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "conditions": [
              {
                "type": "opensiddur:holiday-aggregate",
                "features": {
                  "shabbat": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "condition_instruction": "אַם שַׁבָּת.",
            "condition_instruction_language": "de-Hebr",
            "condition_end_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/6"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "טֹבִים מְאוֹרוֹת שֶׁבָּרָא אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ. יְצָרָם בְּדַֽעַת בְּבִינָה וּבְהַשְׂכֵּל: כֹּחַ וּגְבוּרָה נָתַן בָּהֶם. לִהְיוֹת מוֹשְׁלִים בְּקֶֽרֶב תֵּבֵל: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/3"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "מְלֵאִים זִיו וּמְפִיקִים נֹגַהּ. נָאֶה זִיוָם בְּכָל־הָעוֹלָם: שְׂמֵחִים בְּצֵאתָם וְשָׂשִׂים בְּבוֹאָם. עוֹשִׂים בְּאֵימָה רְצוֹן קוֹנָם: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/4"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "פְּאֵר וְכָבוֹד נוֹתְנִים לִשְׁמוֹ. צָהֳלָה וְרִנָּה לְזֵֽכֶר מַלְכוּתוֹ: קָרָא לַשֶּֽׁמֶשׁ וַיִּזְרַח אוֹר. רָאָה וְהִתְקִין צוּרַת הַלְּבָנָה: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/5"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "שֶֽׁבַח נוֹתְנִים־לוֹ כָּל־צְבָא מָרוֹם. תִּפְאֶֽרֶת וּגְדֻלָּה שְׂרָפִים וְאוֹפַנִּים וְחַיּוֹת הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ:",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/6"
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s103",
                "printed_page": "37",
                "text": "God, Lord above all works, blessed and called blessed by the mouth of every soul, His grandeur and His goodness fill the world, knowledge and understanding surround Him. ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s103",
                "printed_page": "37",
                "text": "He who is exalted above the holy Hayoth, splendid in glory above the Merkabah, merit and equity are",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/2"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "before His throne, grace and compassion before His glory. ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "conditions": [
              {
                "type": "opensiddur:holiday-aggregate",
                "features": {
                  "shabbat": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "condition_instruction": "On Sabbath.",
            "condition_end_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/6"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "Good are the lights which our God has created, He has formed them with knowledge, reason and understanding. Power and strength has He placed in them that they may reign in the midst of the world. ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/3"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "They are full of lustre and brightly shine, comely is their lustre over the whole world. They rejoice when they go forth and are jubilant when they come in and fulfil in awe the will of their Owner. ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/4"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "Glory and honour do they give to His Name, joy and delight at the mention of His Kingdom. He called to the sun, then light shone forth, He saw and decreed the shape of the moon. ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/5"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "Praise does the whole host of heaven bestow on Him, fame and grandeur the Seraphim, Ophanim and holy Hayoth.",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:el_adon/6"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditions": [
        {
          "type": "opensiddur:holiday-aggregate",
          "features": {
            "shabbat": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "lael_asher_shavat": {
      "stem": "lael_asher_shavat",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat",
      "title": {
        "he": "לָאֵל אֲשֶׁר שָׁבַת",
        "en": "To the God who rested"
      },
      "languages": {
        "he": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "לָאֵל אֲשֶׁר שָׁבַת מִכָּל־הַמַּעֲשִׂים בַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי הִתְעַלָּה וְיָשַׁב עַל־כִּסֵּא כְבוֹדוֹ. תִּפְאֶֽרֶת עָטָה לְיוֹם הַמְּנוּחָה עֹנֶג קָרָא לְיוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת: זֶה שֶֽׁבַח שֶׁלַּיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי שֶׁבּוֹ שָׁבַת אֵל מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ: וְיוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי מְשַׁבֵּחַ וְאוֹמֵר ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "מִזְמוֹר שִׁיר לְיוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_1",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/1",
            "reference_unit": "verse",
            "end_reference": true,
            "source_type": "quotation"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "טוֹב לְהוֹדוֹת לַייָ: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/2/a",
            "reference_unit": "prayer-part",
            "end_reference": true,
            "source_type": "quotation",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/2",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/verse/2",
            "source_reference_part": {
              "unit": "half-verse",
              "n": "a",
              "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/verse/2/a"
            }
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "לְפִיכָךְ יְפָאֲרוּ וִיבָרְכוּ לָאֵל כָּל־יְצוּרָיו. שֶֽׁבַח יְקָר וּגְדֻלָּה יִתְּנוּ לָאֵל מֶלֶךְ יוֹצֵר כֹּל הַמַּנְחִיל מְנוּחָה לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּקְדֻשָּׁתוֹ בְּיוֹם שַׁבַּת קֹדֶשׁ: שִׁמְךָ יְיָ אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ יִתְקַדַּשׁ. וְזִכְרְךָ מַלְכֵּֽנוּ יִתְפָּאַר. בַּשָּׁמַיִם מִמַּֽעַל וְעַל־הָאָֽרֶץ מִתָּחַת: תִּתְבָּרַךְ מוֹשִׁיעֵֽנוּ עַל־שֶֽׁבַח מַעֲשֵׂה יָדֶֽיךָ. וְעַל־מְאוֹרֵי־אוֹר שֶׁעָשִֽׂיתָ יְפָאֲרֽוּךָ סֶּֽלָה:",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "To the God who rested from all His works on the seventh day, He rose and was seated on the throne of His glory, He draped Himself in splendour for the day of rest, a delight did He call the Sabbath day. This is the praise of the seventh day that on it God rested from all His work. And the seventh day praises and says: ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "a psalm of the Sabbath day, ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_1",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/1",
            "reference_unit": "verse",
            "end_reference": true,
            "source_type": "quotation"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "it is good to thank the Lord. ",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2",
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/2/a",
            "reference_unit": "prayer-part",
            "end_reference": true,
            "source_type": "quotation",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/2",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/verse/2",
            "source_reference_part": {
              "unit": "half-verse",
              "n": "a",
              "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/lael_asher_shavat/quoted_psalms_92_2/verse/2/a"
            }
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "Therefore do all His creatures glorify and bless God, praise, honour and grandeur do they offer to God, the King, the Creator of all, who has bestowed rest as an inheritance upon His people Israel in His holiness on the Holy Sabbath day. Thy Name. O Lord our God, be sanctified and Thy memory, O our King, be glorified in heaven above and on the earth below. Blessed art Thou, our Helper, for the glory of Thy handiwork and for the radiant lights that Thou hast made, they shall praise Thee, Selah.",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditions": [
        {
          "type": "opensiddur:holiday-aggregate",
          "features": {
            "shabbat": true
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
